<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Setup · <%= portalName %></title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/portal-v2.css"></head>
<body class="auth-body"><main class="auth-shell"><div class="auth-brand"><span class="brand-logo-switch" aria-hidden="true"><img class="brand-logo-dark" src="/icons/portal-logo-dark.svg" alt=""><img class="brand-logo-light" src="/icons/portal-logo-light.svg" alt=""></span><strong><%= portalName %></strong></div><section class="auth-card"><p class="eyebrow">FIRST RUN</p><h1>Connect the portal database</h1><p>The application needs Neon PostgreSQL, session, rate-limit, and integration encryption settings before login is available.</p><ol class="setup-steps"><li>Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code>.</li><li>Set pooled <code>DATABASE_URL</code> and direct <code>DIRECT_URL</code> from Neon.</li><li>Generate independent session, rate-limit, and integration encryption secrets. Production also needs <code>CRON_SECRET</code> and an HTTPS <code>PORTAL_ORIGIN</code>.</li><li>Run <code>npm run db:migrate:dev</code>, then <code>npm run owner:create</code>.</li><li>Optional: set <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> to enable Google sign-in for existing users.</li></ol><a class="button button-primary button-wide" href="/readyz">Check readiness</a><p class="auth-footnote">No default login is created. See README.md for full setup and deployment steps.</p></section></main></body></html>
